extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 8: Japan printed 49-50 (cache p050-p051; text layer, page_offset +1). The Ronin O.C.C. heading is mid-column on printed 49 and the entry ends on printed 50 with the note on experienced samurai; printed 51 opens the Mystic Ninja, so source_book spans 49-50. Printed 50 was rendered and matches the text layer. The ronin defers to the True Samurai for attribute requirements, O.C.C. skills, background skills, training and mastery and equipment; those are read from printed 46-48 (cache p047-p049). || XP: the Ronin, True Samurai column, first table at top left of the Experience Point Tables page (cache p217, folio 216), read off a render: 0 / 2,151 / 4,301 / 8,601 / 17,201 / 25,501 / 36,001 / 52,001 / 73,001 / 98,001 / 134,001 / 184,001 / 240,001 / 295,001 / 385,001. || GROUP: men-of-arms, men_of_arms: true, from the section heading Warrior & Monk Occupational Character Classes (printed 43) and the samurai''s heading Traditional Samurai Warrior O.C.C. No S.D.C. or hit points are printed, so the core values apply; Zanji Shinjinken-Ryo''s +3D6 S.D.C. and attribute bonuses live on its skill row. || ATTRIBUTES: same as the true samurai, I.Q. 9, P.S. 10, P.P. 12, P.E. 10 (printed 48). || P.P.E.: training and mastery item 5, P.E. x2 plus 1D6 per level (printed 47); the female samurai''s P.E. x3 is not stored. || SAVES: +1 vs horror factor at levels 1, 4, 6, 8, 10 and 12, and +1 vs mind control (printed 47). The rune swords'' +1 on all saves, the daisho bonuses and the iron fan''s parry bonus depend on carrying and using those items, so they are prose. || SKILLS: the samurai''s O.C.C. list (printed 48). Horsemanship (+20%) is Horsemanship: General, catalog 40 +20 = 60 at the catalog''s 4 per level; Special Training prints Samurai Horsemanship at 54% +4% per level, which is the older 34% base plus the same 20, so the catalog figure wins and the book''s is in the note. Demon & Monster Lore is Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+15; Tracking is Tracking (people) 25+5; Go 30+10; Calligraphy 35+10; Literacy: Japanese is Literacy: Native Language 40+15; Language: Japanese 98% is Language: Native Tongue; two languages +10% are two Language: Other picks; Mathematics: Basic 45+15. W.P. Samurai Archery is W.P. Bow. Paired Weapons comes from Special Training item 2 and is granted as W.P. Paired Weapons. Two W.P.s of choice are unrestricted: the samurai''s related list limits W.P.s to ancient, but that line is a related-skill rule and the ronin''s related list allows any. || HAND TO HAND: Zanji Shinjinken-Ryo, no alternatives (costs empty). The book''s female samurai takes Kendo and no bow (printed 49); the format cannot switch the style on sex, so this is in the note and here. || BACKGROUND: three family background skills at +10%, a choose group over the union of categories the Family Skills table names (printed 48); the table narrows by background and that pairing is in the note, not enforced. Literacy is filed under Communications in the catalog, so Communications is offered for the two Literacy rows only. The background table itself is a descriptive ability. || RELATED: four, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12, from the ronin''s own list (printed 50). Secondary: three at each of levels two, six and ten from the same list without bonuses, none at level one; the book says select three at levels two, six and ten, read as three per level by analogy with the samurai''s two. || MONEY: none; the ronin starts with only his horse, weapons, armor and clothes, so starting_money is omitted. || EQUIPMENT: the samurai''s basic kit (printed 48): armor, daisho, samurai longbow with 20 regular, 6 silver-tipped and 6 magic arrows, horse, and clothing. The samurai''s other clothing, pack, rations and two extra weapons are not in the ronin''s list. The daisho is daisho-rifts, the ordinary catalog pair; its rune properties are in The Living Samurai Sword ability. Samurai armor and silver-tipped arrows have no catalog row."
